jansson v2.15.1: stop the lexer when a save of the token text fails

Applied by configure-libs.sh after `git checkout "$TAG_JANSSON"`.
Upstream (v2.15.1 and master, 2026-09-23) still has the defect.

The lexer saves every byte of a token in a strbuffer (lex_save), and
ignored the result of strbuffer_append_byte(). When the buffer cannot
grow (the allocator refuses a block: Yuneta routes jansson through
gbmem_*, whose largest block is MEM_MAX_BLOCK), the byte is lost. For a
string token, the saved text then has no closing quote, and
lex_scan_string() decodes it until it finds one: it reads past the end
of the saved text and writes past the end of the decoded string. A heap
overflow, from json text alone: a string longer than about half of the
largest block is enough.

The fix: a failed save puts the stream in the error state (every later
read returns STREAM_STATE_ERROR) and sets the error json_error_out_of_memory.
The other allocation failures of the parser (the decoded string, an
object, an array, a member, an element, a scalar, the lexer buffer) set
json_error_out_of_memory too: before, they returned NULL with no error
text, and a caller could not tell "no memory" from "not json".

